    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #325\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-230-agent-runtime-06-08-record-every-gatew-thr_j5m9q8cfde`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe CI failure was a migration ordinal collision: `develop` had merged a new `0016_agent_run_events_compaction_kind.sql` while this branch's `0016_ai_gateway_calls.sql` was in flight. I rebased onto the latest `develop` and renumbered the new migration to `0018_ai_gateway_calls.sql` (0017 was also already taken by `agent_runs_wake_order.sql`).\n\nNote: an automated merge (`ecf1aab`, from `bb-agent-relay[bot]`) had already landed on the remote branch in the meantime, merging `develop` in without renaming the colliding file — so the collision was still present there. My locally rebased branch contains identical content to that merge commit plus the migration rename, so I force-pushed (`--force-with-lease`) to replace it with the corrected history.\n\nVerified after the fix: full build, unit tests (83/83), integration tests (478/478), e2e tests (5/5), module boundary check, and migration numbering check all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
